spec: S13-06

`export FILE.tar` beside the running harness server: the store goes in as a consistent snapshot
(the note says so), the result line is `FILE  N blobs  SIZE  schema vK`; an existing file is
refused without `--force`; the name must end in `.tar`; `--json`.

```console
$ annotary export backup.tar
export: server running (pid [..]) — the database goes in as a consistent snapshot (SQLite online backup)
backup.tar	[..] blobs	[..]	schema v6

$ annotary export backup.tar
? 5
error: backup.tar exists — --force overwrites it

$ annotary export backup.tar --force --json
export: server running (pid [..]) — the database goes in as a consistent snapshot (SQLite online backup)
{"file":"backup.tar","blobs":[..],"bytes":[..],"schema_version":6}

$ ANNOTARY_TTY=1 annotary export backup.tar --force --json size,live
export: server running (pid [..]) — the database goes in as a consistent snapshot (SQLite online backup)
{"size":"[..]","live":true}

$ annotary export -q backup.tar --force
backup.tar	[..] blobs	[..]	schema v6

$ annotary export backup.tgz
? 1
error: backup.tgz does not end in .tar — export writes an uncompressed tar archive — name it FILE.tar

$ annotary export
? 1
error: the following required arguments were not provided:
  <FILE.tar>

Usage: annotary export <FILE.tar>

For more information, try '--help'.

```
